course: dictionary
lesson: 4061
title: A serious word: genocide
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Genocide is a very serious word. It means the deliberate killing of a large number of people because they belong to a particular nation, ethnic group, race or religion, with the aim of destroying that group. The sentence «South Africa accused Israel of genocide, trying to destroy a whole people» gives you the clue: the word is about trying to destroy a group of people.
explain: Some words are not agreed on by everyone. «Israel strongly rejected the claim» shows that people can disagree about whether this word fits an event. When you read the word, ask who is using it and why. A government, a court or a group may use it, and others may disagree.
explain: Genocide is also a legal word, used in courts. The International Court of Justice is the United Nations' top court, and courts decide whether events count as genocide. That can take years. So when you read a news report, check who made the claim and who disputes it.
fact: Genocide means the deliberate killing of a large number of people because of who they are, with the aim of destroying that group.
fact: Genocide is an international crime, so courts decide whether events count as genocide.
fact: The Holocaust, when the Nazis murdered about six million Jews and others, is the best-known genocide.
fact: In 1932–1933 millions died in Soviet Ukraine in a famine called the Holodomor, which Ukraine and many other countries recognise as genocide.
fact: Some historians debate the legal label, so always say who is making the claim.
exercise: «South Africa accused Israel of genocide, trying to destroy a whole people.» What is the main idea of genocide here? | *Trying to destroy a whole group of people | Building a new town | Making a group famous | Sharing food between two nations
exercise: «Israel strongly rejected the claim.» Why does this show that the word is disputed? | It means the same as famine | It is a word about food | *Only one side uses the word, and the other side says it is wrong | Everyone agreed with it at once
exercise: What do Ukraine and many other countries say about the Holodomor famine? | They say it happened in 1944 in Crimea | It was caused by a flood | It was a big festival | *They recognise it as genocide
test: Which event is the best-known genocide in the lessons? | *The Holocaust, when the Nazis murdered about six million Jews and others | A flood in Rwanda | The Holodomor famine in 1932 | Building the Crimean farms
test: Why should you say who is making a claim about genocide? | Because it makes the word shorter | *Because some governments and courts agree and others disagree | Because the claim is always true | Because genocide is a kind of food
exam: Why is genocide a word that needs careful checking? | It means a small family party | *It is a serious legal word, and people sometimes disagree about whether it fits | It is only used in sport | It is a word for a holiday
